EXT. ABANDONED BOWLING ALLEY - ROOF - DAY

Tar paper and a rusted neon sign shaped like a pin. Three kids sit on the edge, legs swinging, passing a warm soda.

MINA SUNDARESAN (16, ponytail, skateboard on her lap). Her brother JASPER (14, braces) beside her. Their neighbor HOLLIS WADE (17, varsity jacket) stretched out behind them.

                    MINA
          Okay, truth or dare.

                    HOLLIS
          Truth.

                    MINA
          Do you actually like Priscilla, or are you just doing it because everyone expects you to?

                    HOLLIS
          That's two questions.

                    JASPER
          It's one question with two parts.

                    HOLLIS
          Shut up, Jasper.

                    MINA
          Answer.

                    HOLLIS
          I don't know. Maybe I like the idea of her.

                    JASPER
          That's what Dad said about the boat.

                    MINA
          Jasper.

                    JASPER
          What? He sold it.

                    HOLLIS
          Your dad sold the boat?

                    MINA
          Last week. Don't tell anyone.

                    HOLLIS
          I won't.

                    JASPER
          Mina cried.

                    MINA
          I did not.

                    HOLLIS
          It's okay if you did.

                    MINA
          Truth or dare, Hollis. Your turn.

                    HOLLIS
          Dare.

                    MINA
          Jump off the roof.

                    HOLLIS
          Funny.

                    MINA
          Dare you to tell her the truth.

He grins, takes the soda, and finishes it. She smiles. Jasper looks back and forth between them and stays quiet.

                    HOLLIS
          Fine.
